  <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="Tag1" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: sans-serif; margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"&gt;The Company operates an underground natural gas storage facility in Hampshire County, West Virginia that provides storage services exclusively to Washington Gas. The Company is regulated under a cost service tariff by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: sans-serif; margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"&gt;The Company has 100 percent ownership in 25,576 acres of storage leaseholds in Hampshire County, West Virginia. The gas storage operations include twelve injection-withdrawal wells and four observation wells, as well as 18.9 miles of interconnecting pipeline and one compressor station certified to 1,320 horsepower. Additionally, the Company owns a limited interest in 13.1 miles of pipeline, and has limited financial responsibility for potential capital expenditures related to 11.7 miles of pipeline, for a pipeline that provides natural gas transportation service to the Company.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
  <ferc:DescriptionOfPlantAndOperationsOfRespondentTextblock id="Tag2" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;on&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DescriptionOfPlantAndOperationsOfRespondentTextblock>
  <ferc:AdditionalInformationOnFieldsWhereTheRespondentOperatesTextblock id="Tag3" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;on&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:AdditionalInformationOnFieldsWhereTheRespondentOperatesTextblock>
  <ferc:DetailsOfAnyChangesOfScopeInRespondentsOperationsTextblock id="Tag4" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;on&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DetailsOfAnyChangesOfScopeInRespondentsOperationsTextblock>
