&lt;td style="width: 56.1919%; height: 20px; margin-left: 0.1px; border-top: 1pt solid #000000; border-bottom: 1pt solid #000000;" colspan="3"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;Asset retirement obligations at the end of the period&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 22.4806%; height: 20px; margin-left: 0.1px; text-align: right; border-top-width: 1pt; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: #000000; border-bottom-width: 1pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$10,763,326&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; height: 20px; margin-left: 0.1px; text-align: right; border-top-width: 1pt; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: #000000; border-bottom-width: 1pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-color: #000000;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;$10,445,658&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;sup&gt;(a) &lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Hampshire bills Washington Gas for actual settled costs of AROs. Accretion is recorded to Other Regulatory Assets until settlement of such costs&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 2: Pension and Other Post-Retirement Benefit Plans&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Pension Plans&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Washington Gas maintains a qualified, trusteed, non-contributory defined benefit pension plan (qualified plan) covering active and vested former employees of Washington Gas and employees of the Company. The qualified plan was closed to all new hires beginning January 1, 2010. Washington Gas funds pension costs accrued for the qualified plan as required by law. Hampshire is allocated its share of net periodic pension cost and the funded status of the qualified plan based on its percentage of labor costs compared to the combined labor costs of Hampshire and Washington Gas. At December 31, 2025, and 2024, the funded status of pension benefits for Hampshire was a noncurrent asset of $345,720 and $86,663, respectively, which was recorded in &amp;#8220;Miscellaneous Deferred Debits&amp;#8221; on Hampshire&amp;#8217;s balance sheets. Hampshire&amp;#8217;s total pension related costs were income of $28,262 and $30,650 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; color: red; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Other Post-Retirement Benefits&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;Retired employees of the Company are eligible for certain healthcare and life insurance benefits under the Washington Gas Light Company Retiree Health and Welfare Plan sponsored by Washington Gas. Substantially all employees may become eligible for such benefits if they attain retirement status while working for the Company. Hampshire has recorded its allocated share of net periodic post-retirement benefit cost. The funded status is allocated based on labor. The funded status for healthcare and life insurance benefits for Hampshire was a deferred asset of $3,858,555 and $3,029,452 at December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, which was recorded in &amp;#8220;Miscellaneous Deferred Debits&amp;#8221; on Hampshire&amp;#8217;s balance sheets. The total income for other post-retirement benefit plans for the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024 was $762,012 and $1,107,834, respectively. The income allocated to the Company is calculated based on the Company's percentage of labor costs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;During both the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, Washington Gas purchased annual tax-free Medical Health Reimbursement Account (HRA) annuities from an insurance carrier. During the year ended December 31, 2024, Washington Gas also purchased a guaranteed life insurance funding account (GLIFA) from an insurance carrier. These transactions were accounted for as a partial settlement of the Washington Gas Light Company Retiree Health and Welfare Plan. As a result, Hampshire recognized a one-time settlement gain in other income of $350,033 and $624,062, during the year ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;font style="mso-bookmark: _Hlk173411906;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Employee Savings Plans&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;The Company is a participating employer in the Washington Gas Light Company Savings Plan (the Savings Plan) for eligible management employees and the Washington Gas Light Company Capital Appreciation Plan/Union Employees&amp;#8217; Saving Plan (the Capital Appreciation Plan) for eligible union employees. These plans are designed to provide employees with an incentive to save and invest regularly. Both are defined contribution plans, allowing salary deferral by participants from one percent to 50 percent of their salaries (subject to statutory limitations) for investment in various investment options offered by the plans. For the Savings Plan, the Company provides a matching contribution equal to 100 percent of the first four percent of the employees&amp;#8217; compensation contributed on a pre-tax or Roth after-tax basis, or 100 percent of the first three percent contributed on an after-tax basis. For the Capital Appreciation Plan, the Company provides a matching contribution that varies according to terms specified in the applicable union contracts or as otherwise determined by the employer. All employer matching contributions for both plans are invested at the direction of the plan participants. Participants age 50 and older are eligible to make catch-up contributions. There is no employer match for catch-up contributions, and the total catch-up, pre-tax, and after-tax contribution cap is 75%.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Under the Capital Appreciation Plan, union employees hired on or after January 1, 2009, or January 1, 2010, depending on the employee group, receive an employee supplemental contribution equal to 4% of their compensation or the percentage specified in the applicable union contracts.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Under the Savings Plan, management employees first hired on or after July 1, 2009, or who made an irrevocable election in 2009 under the Retirement Choice program to stop earning additional benefits under the Washington Gas Light Employers&amp;#8217; Pension Plan receive an employer supplemental contribution equal to 4% to 6% of their compensation, depending on their years of service beginning January 1, 2010.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The Company contributed a total of $54,408 and $49,003 to the Savings Plan and the Capital Appreciation Plan on behalf of Hampshire employees for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 3: Income Taxes &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;font class="MsoCommentReference"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportAnnotations]--&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 7.0in 7.5in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;Hampshire and WGL&amp;#8217;s other subsidiaries are included in the AltaGas Services (US) Inc. (ASUS) consolidated income tax returns. We have a tax sharing policy with ASUS, an indirect, wholly owned subsidiary of AltaGas, that requires members to pay to ASUS or be reimbursed by ASUS based on that member's tax liabilities and attributes contained in the consolidated return of the group. The financial statements reflect a separate return method as if Hampshire were filing its own separate return. State income tax returns are filed on a separate company basis in most states and on a unitary basis as required, where we or the consolidated ASUS group have operations and/or a requirement to file.&amp;#160; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;At December&amp;#160;31, 2025, Hampshire had a $1,969,249 receivable balance with associated companies under the ASUS tax sharing policy. This receivable balance was settled in January 2026 within the timeline required by the policy. At December 31, 2024, Hampshire did not have any receivable or payable balances with associated companies under the ASUS tax sharing policy.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;The tax sharing balances for the 2023 tax return were settled by December 31, 2024.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Regulatory Treatment of the December 22, 2017 Tax Act&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the balance of the excess and deficient deferred income tax regulatory asset and liability for Hampshire were classified as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 46.7119%; height: 240px;" border="0"&gt;

&lt;tr style="height: 20px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 45.7849%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 26.4556%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 2.90698%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 24.8525%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
