&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The net regulatory liabilities above include protected and unprotected plant related excess deferred income tax amounts that are being passed back to customers over the remaining useful life of the underlying assets giving rise to the associated deferred income taxes (referred to as the Average Rate Assumption Method, &amp;#8220;ARAM&amp;#8221;). The unprotected non-plant related net excess deficient deferred income taxes are being amortized using the Straight-line Method over a period of 10 years. As the excess and deficient deferred income taxes reverse through the amortization periods discussed above, the regulatory assets and liabilities will reverse with an offset to FERC income statement accounts 410.1, Provision of Deferred Income Taxes and 411.1, Provision for Deferred Income Taxes-Credit.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 10.0pt; line-height: 115%; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Components of Income Tax Expense or Benefit &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
