&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 4. Contingencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Hampshire had no recorded litigation nor any material litigation or other claim contingency matters assessed as probable or reasonably possible that would require disclosure in the financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 5. Related Party Transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Hampshire provides storage services exclusively to Washington Gas. The Company operates under a &amp;#8220;pass-through&amp;#8221; cost of service-based tariff approved by FERC and adjusts its billing rates to Washington Gas on a periodic basis to account for changes in its investment in utility plant and associated expenses. For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, total amounts of $10,627,271 and $9,739,539 gas operating revenue were recorded in Hampshire&amp;#8217;s statements of income that were charged to Washington Gas for the gas storage service provided to it. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;In 2001, WGL and its direct and indirect subsidiaries (excluding Washington Gas) entered into a System Money Pool Agreement (Agreement) to provide for certain of their short-term cash and working capital requirements. The Company is a party to the Agreement. Under the terms of the Agreement, participants earn interest on cash contributed to and pay interest on loans received from the System Money Pool. These amounts are recorded in receivables from associated companies and payables to associated companies on the accompanying balance sheets. At December 31, 2025, the Company was in a net receivable position of $745,259 and at December 31, 2024 was in a net payable position of $1,316,004. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;In addition, Hampshire is charged a proportionate share of corporate governance and other shared services costs from AltaGas and Washington Gas primarily related to human resources, employee benefits, legal, accounting, tax, finance, treasury management, information technology services, and other administrative services provided by AltaGas and Washington Gas. Any outstanding balance at the end of the reporting period is recorded into &amp;#8220;Accounts payable to associated companies&amp;#8221; on Hampshire&amp;#8217;s balance sheets.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top: 5.0pt; line-height: 120%; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Refer to Note 3&amp;#8212; Income Taxes for discussions of related party income taxes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note 6: Subsequent Events&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: normal; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;Management has evaluated the impact of events occurring after December 31, 2025, up to&lt;font style="background-color: #ffffff;"&gt; &lt;font style="background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;"&gt;April 17, 2026,&lt;/font&gt; th&lt;/font&gt;e date that these financial statements were available to be issued. These financial statements include all necessary adjustments and disclosures resulting from that evaluation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
